          Yes, and No.  It is not ours in the sense that we signed a 
contract for it, but if possession is 9/10 of the law, then it is at 
least 90% ours.  Just because I believe that doesn't mean - as I infer 
from the tone of your questions - that I believe we shouldn't care for 
it, it just means that any harm we do while learning - defined as you 
will - is far less than many calamities Earth has survived up to now.  
Life is change, not always pleasant.  I care for the environment very 
much, but we are not as important in the geological history of Earth as you 
may believe. 

> 9.  Intellect is the greatest virtue, and creatures with greater intellect
