As I recall, it was originally designed by Seagate (disk mfg) and the first
"S" in the acronym stood for Seagate, not Small.  (They objected to pronouncing
it "scuzzy", they originally pronounced it "sexy".)  When SCSI was adopted as
a standard they reinterpretted the acronym, in much the same way the HPIB
became GPIB...

